{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 176, :comments ["<b>I have gone astray</b> — the meaning is connected to 'revive my soul,' for I am like a lost sheep that relies on the shepherd. And the meaning of 'for I have not forgotten Your commandments': even though I was like a lost sheep, Your commandments were not lost from me."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:02.997230079Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}